  "answer_text": "Found 3 gene records for cystic fibrosis: CF transmembrane conductance regulator [1], Fc gamma receptor IIa [3] and transforming growth factor beta 1 [4], linked to 1 disease: Cystic fibrosis [2]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Cystic fibrosis [2]. \n\nGene-to-disease mapping\n\nGene NCBIGene:1080, name: CF transmembrane conductance regulator [1]. Gene NCBIGene:2212, name: Fc gamma receptor IIa [3]. Gene NCBIGene:7040, name: transforming growth factor beta 1 [4]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Encephalopathy in cystic fibrosis [5]. Pubmed title: 3.22 Nutrition in Cystic Fibrosis [40]. Pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic Fibrosis in Children [42]. Pubmed title: Azithromycin and cystic fibrosis [44]. Pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic fibrosis-related diabetes [46]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Cystic fibrosis [6]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Cystic fibrosis\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Asthma [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Bronchiectasis [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Clubbing of fingers [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Dehydration [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Diarrhea [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Hemoptysis [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Hepatomegaly [13]. Medgen clinical_features: Hepatosplenomegaly [14]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypercalciuria [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Male infertility [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Cirrhosis of liver [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Biliary cirrhosis [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Nasal polyposis [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Pancreatitis [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Cor pulmonale [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Rectal prolapse [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Steatorrhea [23]. Medgen clinical_features: Chronic sinusitis [24]. Medgen clinical_features: Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency [25]. Medgen clinical_features: Recurrent pneumonia [26]. Medgen clinical_features: Chronic lung disease [27]. Medgen clinical_features: Ileus [28]. Medgen clinical_features